keystone_ur is distributed under the licences below.

1. The files derived from the Blockchain Commons bc-ur reference
   implementation are under the BSD-2-Clause Plus Patent License reproduced in
   part A. They are:

     * everything under lib/src/bc_ur/;
     * lib/src/ur.dart, whose UrEncoder and UrDecoder are rewritten from
       bc-ur's ur-encoder.cpp and ur-decoder.cpp;
     * test/bc_ur_test.dart, which ports bc-ur's test suite (test/test.cpp);
     * test/vectors/bc_ur_vectors.dart, the reference vectors from that suite.

   Each of those files says so in its header, and NOTICE lists their
   provenance.

2. lib/src/bc_ur/crc32.dart is a port of bc-ur's src/crc32.c. That file's own
   header puts it under the BSD-2-Clause Plus Patent License, while bc-ur's
   README lists it as BSD-3-Clause. Both texts are reproduced, in parts A and
   C, so a copy that carries this file meets the conditions of either.

3. Every other file in this package is under the MIT License reproduced in
   part B, the same licence as the rest of the mallow wallet repository.

The test vectors in test/vectors/keystone_vectors.dart come from Keystone's
MIT- and ISC-licensed repositories; NOTICE names them and reproduces their
licence texts.

